  "doc": "Hollowmere's townsfolk at the Ch15 dawn (B11: the people the Order burned, looking at Toma's pauldron; the Lead, 2026-10-30: Act II crowds from the bodies that exist). Saltwright crowd people (crowd.json, the saltwright community) on the hull-house platforms and along the dock's edges, clear of the walkway and the story marks (fathers_door, supper, confess_*). The greybox names no actors here, so each row's `at` makes its stand-in at CrowdSpots/<id> (VillagerLayer). Liss's father, the brine-branded old woman and the widow are the characters track's named people, not these. The vignettes at the Ch15 dawn (the Lead, 2026-10-30: the Act II towns lived in; ground probed 2026-10-30): the work of the morning after the burning, no games: a man hauling a salvage line at the dock's edge, a man carrying a basket of what was saved, an old man mending a scorched net on his platform, a girl folding the cloths her family saved.",
